        <!-- Seed43 theming: this file used to alias its own local colour
             names (BgWindow/Accent/TextMain/etc) to the canonical Brush*
             names via a bridging step in LayoutSettingsWindow.__init__
             (see _apply_seed43_theme in LayoutSettings.py) - that's been
             eliminated. Every DynamicResource reference below now points
             directly at the same canonical names apply_seed43_palette()/
             apply_seed43_dimensions() inject, matching pyTransmit and
             About - no local declaration for those exists in this file at
             all any more, so if seed43_palette.json is ever missing, these
             DynamicResource lookups simply resolve to nothing rather than
             falling back to a second, separately-maintained hardcoded copy.

             LocalBrushRowBg/LocalBrushHoverBg/LocalBrushBorderNeutral and
             ColA-D are the exception: no canonical token exists yet for a
             neutral (non-accent) border/row colour, and ColA-D are
             intentional, distinct functional markers for the 4 layout
             columns, not theme colours - forcing them onto a single shared
             accent colour would destroy the whole point of them being
             different colours. These four stay as real local declarations,
             genuinely needed (not "double code"), and are candidates worth
             promoting into seed43_palette.json later if other tools want
             the same neutral-border/row-tint pattern.

             LocalBrushTextMuted is injected in code instead of declared
             here - see _apply_seed43_theme - since it's computed
             (BrushTextPrimary at reduced opacity), not a fixed value. -->
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="LocalBrushRowBg"    Color="#323D4D"/>
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="LocalBrushHoverBg"  Color="#3A4760"/>
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="LocalBrushBorderNeutral" Color="#404E62"/>
